# Let the SM8550/SM8650 Type-C USB controller (dwc3-qcom) runtime-suspend.
#
# The driver leaves runtime PM "on", so with nothing plugged in the
# controller stays active in device role for good and holds an xm_usb3_0
# DDR vote of 1 GB/s avg / 2.5 GB/s peak.
#
# HW-checked on the KONKR Pocket FIT, 2026-10-14: with "auto" it suspends
# 5 s after unplug and the vote drops to 0/0; plugging a hub in wakes it
# through the Type-C role switch, which goes host and enumerates at
# SuperSpeed, same as with "on". Idle battery draw was unchanged there (the
# display's DDR vote dominates). On the AYANEO Pocket ACE (SM8550), same
# vote, idle battery V x I 3x30 s each: 2653 mW -> 2592 mW (~60 mW, 2.3%).
#
# Scope. Only the Type-C port's controller; the built-in pad on SM8650 hangs
# off a PCIe xHCI and is not touched. A device in use keeps the controller
# active, so this adds no per-input latency.
ACTION=="add|bind", SUBSYSTEM=="platform", DRIVER=="dwc3-qcom", ENV{OF_COMPATIBLE_0}=="qcom,sm8550-dwc3|qcom,sm8650-dwc3", ATTR{power/control}="auto"
